{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_9fc65dcc89d08e41e4114d01","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"minimax-m3.1-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now the real bug. Expected: 100 NOK + 10 EUR = 215.0. EUR rate is 11.50 NOK per unit. So 10 EUR = 115 NOK. Total 215.\n\nBut `to_nok` does `amount / nok_per_unit(currency)` — divides. That's the bug: NOK_PER_UNIT is NOK per one unit of foreign currency, so conversion must multiply.\n\nWait, but SEK is 1.00 and USD 10.80. The rate table says \"NOK per one unit of the foreign currency.\" So amount_in_nok = amount * rate. Division is wrong.\n\nLet me verify: 10 / 11.50 = 0.87, + 100 = 100.87 ≠ 215. Correct: 10 * 11.5 = 115, + 100 = 215. ✓\n\nSo the fix is in billing/currency.py: multiply instead of divide. That's the root cause in the billing package.\n\nLet me check whether the round placement matters. to_nok rounds per line to 2 decimals; report sums rounded lines then rounds. That's fine-ish. Keep it.\n\nAlso check: is there rounding subtleties? to_nok rounds to 2 decimals — fine.\n\nLet me apply the fix.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":22368,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60bc1fb0-ea8e-4be5-ba5b-5035250e66dc","uuid":"dbc03f9b-56cf-45bf-8cb8-4337aceccd26","timestamp":"2026-10-30T13:07:47.553Z","thinking_duration_ms":2000,"thinking_display":"updates"}
